<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="106" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>ISS-008 (#973) — a re-grant over an EXPIRED survivor judges "confers access" across every active row on the key before answering 409</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (owner rule 2026-09-15)</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Grant write path (.cs, Api/ExternalAccess); tags bff-api/auth.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Localized change to one endpoint's match path with existing expiry logic to reuse; the contract judgment point is an escalation trigger.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Api/ExternalAccess/** is parallel-unsafe in this project (project CLAUDE.md).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>—</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Register ISS-008 / GitHub #973 — kept in the project under the owner's 2026-09-15 rule: material (a wrong access answer on this project's grant endpoint).</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>In GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.CreateGrantAsync's match path, when the elected survivor (lowest id) is expired and the request carries no new expiry, the endpoint returns 409 sdap.grant.expired_not_restored ("still confers no access") BEFORE CollapseDuplicatesAsync runs. If another active row on the same key has a later or null expiry, the grantee does have access — the 409 is false. Duplicates are real in dev (task 097 notes: one contact, five rows, one matter).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, C#/.NET, the external grant lifecycle.</role>
  <goal>The match path computes "does this grant confer access" across every active row on the key; 409 expired_not_restored is returned only when no active row on the key confers access; duplicate collapse never deactivates the row that confers access.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Register ISS-008 (task 097 code review; pre-existing since task 023). The read side's definition of "expired" is task 007's ExpiryPredicate (DateOnly); sprk_expiresdate is Date Only and null means never-expiring on the read path.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs — CreateGrantAsync (:178), the 409 (:143), CollapseDuplicatesAsync (:402)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-023-grant-upsert-expiry.md and notes/task-097-*.md — the expired-survivor rule and the duplicates evidence</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="register ISS-008">Scope: the fix. NOT "collapse first" — collapsing onto an expired survivor would revoke live access.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every answer. Fail closed: an outcome the endpoint cannot verify is never reported as success.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: expiry. Reuse the read path's expiry definition; do not write a second one.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: response contract. Status codes and reasonCodes are unchanged; needing a new one is an escalation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement Justification (existing endpoint); publish size against a fresh master.</constraint>
    <constraint source="review-2026-08-24">Scope: verification. Perturbation is mandatory; pair positives with negatives.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Read CreateGrantAsync end to end and verify the register's description against the code.</step>
    <step order="1">Judge "confers access" across all active rows on the key — or elect the survivor with the latest effective expiry. Choose the option that keeps the response contract; record why in the notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Make sure the collapse keeps the row that confers access.</step>
    <step order="3">Tests (KEEP path) for the closed set below; perturbations; build, full suite, publish size; notes/task-106-regrant-expired-survivor.md; TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the honest response when a live duplicate exists needs a status code or reasonCode the contract does not have, STOP and escalate with options.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/ (KEEP path)</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-106-regrant-expired-survivor.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Expired survivor plus an active duplicate with a LATER expiry, request without a new expiry → no 409; the response does not claim "no access".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Same with a NULL-expiry duplicate → no 409 (null is never-expiring on the read path).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Regression: expired survivor with no conferring duplicate → 409 sdap.grant.expired_not_restored, unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: after the call the row that conferred access is still active (the collapse did not deactivate it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a request that carries a new expiry behaves exactly as before (the task 023 path).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Perturbation: restoring the survivor-only check fails at least one test; collapsing onto the lowest id regardless of expiry fails at least one test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build green; full suite green; publish size reported against a fresh master and ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Register ISS-008; GitHub #973 (label unified-access-control-r2). Related: tasks 010, 023, 097.</notes>

  <completion date="2026-09-18" session="15">
    <summary>
      The match path now judges "confers access" across every active row on the key. The fix is the
      ELECTION, not the check: the survivor is the row conferring access longest (ConferralRank), ties
      broken by ascending id. Three properties become structural rather than checked — an expired survivor
      proves every row is expired; the collapse cannot deactivate the conferring row, because that row IS
      the survivor; and a request carrying an explicit expiry behaves as it always did. The naive fix
      (suppress the 409 and fall through) would have REVOKED the live access it had just detected, turning
      an inert bug destructive; that is why the register said "NOT collapse first".
    </summary>
    <commits>3d1ce86e6, b849cf6e7, e17a4c1c9, 97481c917, 3750bf269</commits>
    <escalation-trigger fired="false">
      The honest response when a live duplicate exists is 200 plus the surviving row id — both already in
      the contract. No status code or reasonCode was added, changed, or removed. Checked, not assumed.
    </escalation-trigger>
    <step-9-5 outcome="found-a-regression-this-task-introduced">
      adr-check 1 violation / 9 warnings; code-review 1 Critical / 6 Warning / 8 Suggestion. BOTH gates
      independently found the same Critical defect (V1 / F1): the first version ranked rows by a
      PER-REQUEST value, so the election was not a total order two callers share. Two concurrent grants
      could elect different survivors and deactivate each other, leaving ZERO active rows while both
      received HTTP 200. Pre-106 that interleaving was impossible, so it was strictly worse than the false
      409 it replaced. Fixed in e17a4c1c9 by ranking on ConferralRank and REMOVING the request parameter,
      making request-independence structural. Also fixed: F6 (a stale comment five lines from my own
      edit), F2 (my own false "must not merge" claim), F4 (one name for two values), F9 (two tests missing
      a precondition the notes claimed all had), F3 (a second in-memory expiry copy, folded in), F11 (an
      unenforced precondition). Filed rather than fixed: ISS-022 (F5) and ISS-023 (F10).
    </step-9-5>
    <verification>
      build 0/0 (--no-incremental); affected classes 52/52 with the expected count derived from source
      attributes independently of the run; perturbations 5/5 CAUGHT, 0 MISSED, 0 INVALID (spread
      7/5/1/1/2); ArchTests 323/323 (count unchanged); Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests 12,501/0/58; Spaarke.Core.Tests
      64/64; Spaarke.Scheduling.Tests 75/75; Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests compiles; publish 45.46 MB vs
      RE-MEASURED master 45.35 = +0.11 MB with 214 files each side (task 106's own increment about
      +0.01 MB); no vulnerable packages, no package added.
    </verification>
    <record>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-106-regrant-expired-survivor.md</record>
  </completion>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
